# ChatJuridico Global Standards

> Canonical source: `chatjuridico-devkit/CLAUDE.md` · Skills: `~/.cursor/skills/cj-*`

## Non-negotiables

1. Tenant isolation — scope every query by `office_id`; never bypass Supabase RLS.
2. No PII in logs or LLM output.
3. LGPD compliance on all personal data.
4. UI copy in pt-BR; code in English.
5. No secrets in source; no `console.log` in production.

## How to work

- Minimal diff; solve the asked problem only.
- Read surrounding code; match existing conventions.
- No over-engineering or premature abstraction.
- Only commit when explicitly asked.
- Branch names use hyphens: `feature-nome`.

## When stuck

Use devkit skills: `cj-code-review`, `cj-systematic-debugging`, `cj-writing-plans`.
